{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make it a legal requirement for shops to provide customer bathroom facilities",
        "additional_details": "People with IBS, Crohn\u2019s disease, disabilities and other medical conditions can experience sudden, urgent bathroom needs. Being refused access can cause severe distress, humiliation and potentially accidents in public. I have personally experienced this despite explaining my disability. No one should face this indignity. I believe shops should be legally required to provide customer bathrooms, with accessible facilities and reasonable exemptions, to protect people\u2019s health, dignity and equality.",
        "background": "I want the Government to introduce legislation requiring all retail shops to provide bathroom facilities for customers, including accessible facilities for disabled people and those with urgent medical conditions such as IBS and Crohn\u2019s disease, with reasonable exemptions where necessary.",
